WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.310
Some of the most talented performers of all
time reached the end of the road doing what

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:10.110
they loved: making movies and television for
devoted viewers across the globe.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.440
Their sudden passing while on the job left
their castmates reeling and fans heartbroken.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.710
Here are a few stars both young and old whose
lives were cut short while they were hard

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.950
at work.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.120
Redd Foxx

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:27.640
On his classic '70s sitcom Sanford and Son,
Redd Foxx was famous for faking a heart attack

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:29.700
to get out of a conversation.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.130
And audiences loved it.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.560
"This is the big one.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.560
I'm dying.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.580
Ya hear that, Elizabeth?

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.100
I'm comin to join ya honey."

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:43.559
Foxx brought the bit out of retirement when
he returned to TV in 1991 with a sitcom called

00:00:43.559 --> 00:00:44.899
The Royal Family.

00:00:44.899 --> 00:00:49.510
But during rehearsal, according to production
spokeswoman Rachel McCallister, Foxx and his

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:50.510
co-stars were:

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:54.229
"Clowning around, and Redd was sort of breaking
people up when he collapsed.

00:00:54.229 --> 00:00:56.449
[…] They all thought he was joking at first."

00:00:56.449 --> 00:01:02.559
Four hours later at the hospital, Foxx passed
away at age 68 of a heart attack.

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:03.920
Jon-Erik Hexum

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:09.890
Twenty-six-year-old heartthrob Jon-Erik Hexum
starred in Cover Up, a CBS action show in

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:12.660
which he played an elite military operative.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:18.470
One day in October 1984, the producers told
Hexum that scheduling issues would delay filming,

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:21.930
so he grabbed a prop gun and quipped, "Can
you believe this crap?"

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:24.140
Then he pulled the trigger.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.000
Prop master Frank Laux remembered,

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.960
"He unloaded all but I guess one round."

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:32.520
"What would appear to be a game of Russian
roulette, put it up to his head and pulled

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.580
the trigger."

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:39.550
The prop gun fired a cotton wad bullet, driving
a bone fragment into his brain, which caused

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:40.780
severe hemorrhaging.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:45.170
The actor was rushed to the hospital, where
he fell into a coma, and passed away six days

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:46.730
later.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:47.730
John Ritter

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:52.880
While he had a successful film career with
roles in Sling Blade and Bad Santa, John Ritter

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.170
will forever rank among our most beloved and
prolific TV actors.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.060
"She's gonna send you bowling."

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.220
"I don't bowl!"

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.820
"I'm supposed to teach you!"

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:11.200
His likability and gift for physical comedy
helped elevate Three's Company, and his return

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:16.550
to TV in 2002 as the star of 8 Simple Rules
for Dating My Teenage Daughter was one of

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.240
the biggest stories of the year.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:24.340
ABC had renewed the sitcom for a second season,
and production was underway in September 2003

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:29.380
when Ritter suddenly fell ill on set, feeling
dizzy and nauseated while complaining of chest

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:30.380
pains.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:34.670
Ritter checked in to a hospital in Burbank,
where doctors treated him for what they initially

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:35.780
thought was a heart attack.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:41.560
But further tests revealed a previously undiagnosed
aortic dissection, which proved fatal for

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:42.560
Ritter.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.540
He was just 54 years old.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:45.770
Steve Irwin

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:51.020
Famously known as "The Crocodile Hunter,"
Steve Irwin was the enthusiastic, Australian

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:55.780
nature show host who boldly ventured into
hostile environments to teach viewers about

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.420
dangerous and exotic creatures.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:03.590
"You can see why they call them tiger… tiger
rattlesnakes."

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:08.660
But in September 2006, as Irwin and crew were
filming a documentary about the Great Barrier

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:14.890
Reef in Australia, Irwin and cameraman Justin
Lyons encountered an eight-foot-wide stingray,

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:16.290
which attacked Irwin.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:20.870
Lyons said the creature launched "hundreds
of strikes in a few seconds," delivering a

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:25.430
fatal dose of venom and a two-inch-wide gash
over Irwin's heart.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:26.780
He was 44 years old.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:27.959
Tommy Cooper

00:03:27.959 --> 00:03:33.440
A beloved British entertainer, Tommy Cooper
combined corny jokes, prop comedy, and magic

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.370
for an act that was popular in the U.K. for
decades.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:42.110
But tragedy struck in April 1984 when Cooper
appeared on the Live from Her Majesty's variety

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.110
show.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:47.190
The show's host Jimmy Tarbuck, and likely
many viewers of the live broadcast, thought

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.680
Cooper was improvising when he fell to the
ground.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:52.320
But the entertainer had suffered a heart attack.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.370
The show cut to commercial, and Cooper was
rushed to a hospital, where he passed away

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.480
at age 63.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:00.430
Tyrone Power

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:05.540
Having enjoyed a meteoric rise to superstardom
in the 1930s, Tyrone Power's breakthrough

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:11.350
role in Lloyd's of London came in 1936 when
he was just 22 years old.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:16.250
He went on to establish himself as an extremely
versatile actor, but was most often cast in

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:20.060
swashbuckling adventure movies such as The
Mask of Zorro.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:24.530
In 1958, Power landed a title role in Solomon
and Sheba.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:30.000
But on November 11, 1958, as Power shot the
eighth take of a demanding sword fighting

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.590
scene, he started to shake, and said he suddenly
felt chilly and achy.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:39.270
Power passed away en route to the hospital,
having suffered a fatal heart attack at age

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.270
44.

